ftext|><|endoftext|><|endof\n","text|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|>\n","<|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endo\n","ftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|> \n","\n","*** Example:\n"," QUESTION: ELI5: When a comet or an asteroid passes close to Earth, how scientists determine the chance it will hit Earth?\n","ANSWER: Astronomers analyze newly discovered asteroids to determine whether its orbit around the sun could bring it close\n","to the Earth[1]. They take successive images of the asteroid over the course of days after its discovery in order to\n","predict its probable orbital path for the near future. The chance of an impact depends on the size of the object; the\n","bigger the comet or asteroid, the smaller the chance, since there are many more small objects out there than large ones[2].\n","The risk of an asteroid hitting Earth is ranked on the Torino scale, which goes from zero (lowest risk) to 10 (highest\n","risk)[3]. The team also looks for asteroids with orbits that safely remain completely interior to Earth’s orbit and\n","shouldn’t ever come in its path[4]. The next asteroid of substantial size to potentially hit Earth is 2005 ED224, and there\n","is roughly a 1 in 500,000 chance of impact[2][5].<|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endofte\n","xt|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|\n","endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoft\n","ext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><\n","|endoftext|> \n","\n","*** Example:\n"," QUESTION: Mineral Frakking ANSWER: Mineral fracturing, or fracking, is a well stimulation technique involving the\n","fracturing of bedrock formations by a pressurized liquid. The process involves the high-pressure injection of a fracking\n","fluid, which typically contains water, sand, or other proppants suspended with the aid of thickening agents, into a\n","wellbore to create cracks in the deep-rock formations, allowing natural gas, petroleum, and brine to flow more freely[3].\n","Sand is the most commonly used proppant, with high-purity quartz, or frac sand, being the most prized for its round shape,\n","uniform size, and crush resistance[4]. Fracking is also used to refer specifically to the fracturing processes involved in\n","the extraction of gas and oil from sedimentary rock such as shale[5].<|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|\n","endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoft\n","ext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><\n","|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endof\n","text|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|>\n","<|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endo\n","ftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|\n","><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|end\n","oftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext\n","|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|><|endoftext|> \n","\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["tokenizer.decode(train_tokens[np.random.randint(train_tokens.shape[0])